---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import config from "../../site.config";
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What Property Desk records: one enquiry form, cookieless visitor counts, and nothing else. No account, no advertising trackers, no profiling." path="/privacy">
  <div class="col" style="padding-block: var(--space-l) var(--space-xl);">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">The enquiry form</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      One form on this site collects anything: the enquiry form. It asks for
      your name, email and phone, and optionally what you are trying to work
      out. We store what you send along with the date, your IP address and the
      exact wording of the consent you agreed to, because a consent you cannot
      evidence is not a consent.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use it to introduce you to a licensed broker. We are paid for that
      introduction, which is stated at the bottom of every page. We do not sell
      your details to a list, and there is no newsletter, no account and no
      sign-in.
    </p>
    <p>
      Enquiries are deleted after 24 months. You can ask us to delete yours
      sooner by replying to any message we send you.
    </p>
    <p>
      The map runs entirely in your browser. Which community you click, which
      period you choose and which areas you compare are never sent anywhere.
      They are not stored, not logged and not counted.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">What is recorded</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      We set no advertising cookies and run no advertising trackers. Our host
      records ordinary web server logs, including IP addresses, in order to
      serve the site and absorb abuse. We do not combine those with anything
      else and do not use them to identify anyone.
    </p>
    <p>
      The basemap is served by OpenFreeMap, so your browser requests map tiles
      from them directly and they see those requests, as any provider of an
      image on a page would.
    </p>
    <p>
      We count visits using Vercel Web Analytics and measure how quickly pages
      load using Vercel Speed Insights. Both are run by our host, both are
      cookieless, and neither writes anything to your device or follows you to
      any other site. They record the page you viewed, roughly where in the
      world the request came from, and how the page performed. There is no
      identifier that links one visit of yours to another, and we cannot pick
      an individual reader out of either.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">The data on the map is not about you</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      Everything shown is aggregate: medians and counts across whole
      communities, computed from the Dubai Land Department's published
      transaction register. No buyer, seller or owner is named anywhere on this
      site, and no individual property is identified.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">Your rights</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      Under the UAE Personal Data Protection Law you may ask what is held about
      you, and ask for it to be corrected or deleted. If you have never sent an
      enquiry, there is nothing of yours here to return: the visitor counts
      above carry no identifier that could be traced back to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      If what we collect changes, this page changes with it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
